{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"112260","commit":"266b8845217fcf7c29dd6a3583c91d5ff3f88167","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change from an array to a map for `leaves` introduces potential performance implications. Accessing elements by index in an array is O(1), whereas accessing elements by key in a map is generally O(log n) due to the underlying data structure (assuming a balanced tree). Additionally, the use of `ConcurrentCollections.newConcurrentMap()` implies that the map is thread-safe, but this comes with additional overhead compared to a regular `HashMap`. Ensure that the performance characteristics of using a map here are acceptable given the expected usage patterns.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/lookup/StoredFieldSourceProvider.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/lookup/StoredFieldSourceProvider.java-1324:1408,1421:1436,1460:1543,1556:1576,1589:1604,1707:1722-1417:1444,1453:1483,1496:1504,1528:1536,1528:1536,1626:1674,1687:1761,1787:1795,1787:1795","promptId":"#4DY5X","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/lookup/StoredFieldSourceProvider.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/lookup/StoredFieldSourceProvider.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1324,"endPos":1408,"startLine":32,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":32,"endLineOffset":92,"length":85},{"pos":1421,"endPos":1436,"startLine":33,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":33,"endLineOffset":27,"length":16},{"pos":1460,"endPos":1543,"startLine":34,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":34,"endLineOffset":95,"length":84},{"pos":1556,"endPos":1576,"startLine":35,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":35,"endLineOffset":32,"length":21},{"pos":1589,"endPos":1604,"startLine":36,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":36,"endLineOffset":27,"length":16},{"pos":1707,"endPos":1722,"startLine":38,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":38,"endLineOffset":30,"length":16}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1417,"endPos":1444,"startLine":33,"startLineOffset":8,"endLi